{
  "title": "SolidTexel",
  "description": "A fully opaque point in a glyph source's texture, addressed as a single texel rather than a rectangle. Text decorations are plain filled quads and need somewhere in the atlas that reads as solid ink at every sample. A degenerate UV is what makes that hold under linear filtering: every sample of the quad reads the same texel, so no neighbouring glyph can bleed into a rule's edge.",
